    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "88guylu",
      "content": "Medical‑Surgical Nursing focuses on the care of adult patients with medical conditions or those undergoing surgical procedures. It covers assessment, diagnosis, treatment, and nursing management of disorders affecting major body systems. In competitive nursing examinations such as RRB Nursing, questions frequently appear from cardiovascular, respiratory, gastrointestinal, renal, neurological, and endocrine disorders along with nursing care principles."
    },
